<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 7 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Explorers and Travellers</h1><p class="path-tagline">Seven journeys that stitched the world together.</p><p class="path-intro">Before the world was mapped it was walked, ridden and sailed, often by people who had little idea what lay ahead. This path follows seven travellers whose journeys, and whose accounts of them, changed what the world knew about itself.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Navigator</a> · <a href="/start">the Chronicler</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/xuanzang"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xuanzang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Person · 602–664</span><span class="path-step-name">Xuanzang</span><span class="path-step-why">The Tang monk who walked to India for scriptures and came back a legend.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marco-polo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Person · 1275–1292 in China</span><span class="path-step-name">Marco Polo</span><span class="path-step-why">A Venetian in the service of Kublai Khan, whose book gave Europe its picture of Asia.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Person · 1334–1341 at Delhi</span><span class="path-step-name">Ibn Battuta</span><span class="path-step-why">Thirty years and some 120,000 kilometres across the Islamic world and beyond.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zheng-he.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Person</span><span class="path-step-name">Zheng He</span><span class="path-step-why">Treasure fleets to Arabia and Africa, decades before Europe rounded the Cape.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Person</span><span class="path-step-name">Christopher Columbus</span><span class="path-step-why">Four voyages that joined two worlds and began a catastrophe and an age at once.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Person · 1498</span><span class="path-step-name">Vasco da Gama</span><span class="path-step-why">The sea road to India, and the gun-backed trade empire that followed it.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 1480–1521</span><span class="path-step-name">Ferdinand Magellan</span><span class="path-step-why">The expedition that proved the world round by sailing it, though its commander never came home.</span></span></a></li></ol>
